------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Game import: archive and game-file reading
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Used by the main app (Library tab) to read games straight from archives and disc images. All are compatible with GPL-3.0.

- libarchive — https://libarchive.org — New BSD licence. Reads RAR (RAR 4 and RAR 5) archives.
- libarchive-android (Java/JNI bindings and Android build of libarchive) by Hai Zhang —
  https://github.com/zhanghai/libarchive-android — Apache License 2.0. It bundles libarchive with zlib,
  bzip2 (BSD-style), liblzma (0BSD / public domain), lz4 (BSD 2-Clause), zstd (BSD) and Mbed TLS (Apache 2.0).
- Apache Commons Compress — https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-compress/ — Apache License 2.0.
  Reads zip, 7z, tar, gzip and xz archives.
- XZ for Java — https://tukaani.org/xz/java.html — 0BSD / public domain. Used by Commons Compress for xz and 7z.

Emulation cores that play the imported games are credited on the About screen and in UPSTREAM-README.md:
Mupen64Plus / Mupen64Plus-AE (N64), bsnes (SNES), PPSSPP (PSP) and Dolphin (GameCube).

No game, BIOS or ROM is distributed with VictorLink64. Bring your own legally obtained games.

